  #line-at(171.416pt, 249.12pt, "a")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(173.916pt, 252.24pt, "Rapiscan Systems GmbH, Heinz-Fangman-Str. 4, 42287 Wuppertal, Germany ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 294pt, "Abstract ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 310.32pt, "Organic scintillators using a solid polyurethane (PU) matrix have been introduced to combine the robustness of a construction ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 325.92pt, "material with scintillating properties that allow gamma rays and fast neutrons to be detected efficiently and at low cost. This ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 341.28pt, "work compares two corresponding materials, the older M600 and the more recent M700, with EJ-276D and EJ-200 representing ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 356.88pt, "common plastic scintillators with and without pulse-shape discrimination (PSD) capabilities, respectively. Characterization ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 372.48pt, "measurements were performed with small samples of 26 mm diameter and 10 mm height, which were coupled to a ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 388.08pt, "photomultiplier tube (PMT) and simultaneously exposed to ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(288.061pt, 384.96pt, "252")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(297.061pt, 388.08pt, "Cf fission neutrons and ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(384.618pt, 384.96pt, "137")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(393.618pt, 388.08pt, "Cs gamma rays. M700 turned out to ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 403.44pt, "provide the best PSD performance and about the same light yield as EJ-276D, while its light pulses exhibit a shorter pulse decay. ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 419.04pt, "An accelerated ageing process applied in between two test campaigns was too short to trigger distinct performance degradation ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 434.64pt, "in any of the materials, though optical degradation was visible in EJ-276D and in EJ-200 but not in the PU-based materials. ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 450pt, "Nevertheless, the extremely robust polyurethane matrix promises advantages in medical and industrial applications where ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 465.6pt, "resilience and long-term stability are of crucial importance. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 486.24pt, "Keywords: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(106.264pt, 486.24pt, "Scintillator, fast neutron, gamma ray, pulse-shape discrimination, polyurethane, ageing. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 537.36pt, "1.")
  #line-at(80.906pt, 537.36pt, "Introduction ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(81.6pt, 562.32pt, "Solid organic scintillators have been used to measure neutron and gamma radiation for more than half ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 581.28pt, "a century [1]-[2]. Their hydrogen content makes them sensitive to fast neutrons, as (elastic) neutron ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 600.24pt, "scattering on hydrogen nuclei – consisting of a single proton – generates fast recoil protons and ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 619.2pt, "corresponding ionization tracks within the scintillator, which are easily detected. Gamma detection in ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 638.16pt, "organic scintillators is basically due to Compton scattering, as low charge numbers of the scintillators’ ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 657.12pt, "constituents make photoabsorption quite improbable. Consequently, energy spectra of gamma rays ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 676.08pt, "measured with plastic scintillators do not exhibit photopeaks but characteristic Compton edges, at least ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 697.2pt, "——— ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 704.16pt, "*")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.6pt, 707.28pt, " Corresponding author. e-mail: gpausch@rapiscan.com ")
]

