#original-page(595.2pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(228.055pt, 116.4pt, "Paper submitted to ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(290.047pt, 116.4pt, "Radiation Measurement ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 116.4pt, "2 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 143.04pt, "in the energy range of 30 keV to 3 MeV, which is the most interesting one for many applications. This ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 162pt, "and the moderate light yield of common plastic materials (around 10 photons / keV [3]), which cannot ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 180.96pt, "compete with that of inorganic crystals as NaI(Tl) or LaBr")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(355.28pt, 181.92pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(358.78pt, 180.96pt, "(Ce) (about 45 to 76 photons/keV, ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 199.92pt, "respectively [4]), result in a poor spectroscopic performance. However, plastic scintillators can be ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 218.88pt, "produced in large sizes and are quite affordable. Their unrivaled sensitivity per cost (counts per second ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 237.84pt, "and dollar of detector investment in a given radiation field) makes them attractive for many applications ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 256.8pt, "in homeland security, industry, or medicine.  ")
  #line-at(81.6pt, 281.76pt, "The favorable sensitivity-to-cost ratio is the reason why large-volume plastic scintillators have been ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 300.72pt, "used in Radiation Portal Monitors (RPMs), built to disclose potentially illicit transportation of radioactive ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 319.68pt, "material through points of entrance (POE) by measuring gamma radiation emitted from the cargo. ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 338.64pt, "However, ageing effects in common polyvinyl toluene (PVT) scintillators – especially the so-called ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 357.6pt, "“fogging” by exposure to humidity in combination with large temperature variations – turned out to be ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 376.56pt, "a weak point limiting the lifetime of corresponding detectors [5]. This issue motivated Target ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 395.52pt, "Systemelektronik")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(146.64pt, 390.96pt, "1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(150.189pt, 395.52pt, " some years ago to start research in plastic scintillators. The initial question was: Is it ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 414.48pt, "possible to provide extremely robust and rugged plastic materials as used in civil engineering or machine ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 433.44pt, "construction with scintillating properties? Corresponding efforts [6] lead to a first suitable polyurethane-")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 452.4pt, "(PU-)based scintillator material named M600, available since 2018, which exhibits not only reasonable ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 471.36pt, "light yield but also quite decent pulse-shape discrimination (PSD) capabilities [7]. The latter is an ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 490.56pt, "inestimable advantage, as it allows to discriminate neutron signals (recoil protons) against gamma ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 509.52pt, "detections (recoil electrons) and thus to find neutron signatures in a gamma background, which is ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 528.48pt, "important for a doubtless detection and identification of Special Nuclear Materials (SNM). Note that the ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 547.44pt, "most common solid organic scintillators including those used in RPMs cannot distinguish neutron- from ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 566.4pt, "gamma-induced events. ")
  #line-at(81.6pt, 591.36pt, "PSD-capable plastic scintillators had been developed [8] and marketed before PU-based materials ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 610.32pt, "were available. An early commercial product, the Eljen E-J276, could provide reasonable discrimination ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 629.28pt, "(see e.g. [9]) but suffered from ageing in terms of a significant reduction of light yield over time [10]. ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 648.24pt, "Meanwhile, several new materials have been developed and introduced [11]-[12], in particular organic ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 667.2pt, "glass scintillators (OGS) [13]-[14] which outperform other plastic scintillators in terms of light yield and ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 684.96pt, "——— ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 692.88pt, "1")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(75.739pt, 696.48pt, "Target Systemelektronik GmbH & Co. KG, Heinz-Fangman-Str. 4, 42287 Wuppertal, Germany, recently merged with ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 707.28pt, "Rapiscan Systems GmbH, Frankfurt.")
]

// arXiv source page 3
#original-page(595.2pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(231.163pt, 116.4pt, "Paper submitted to ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(293.155pt, 116.4pt, "Radiation Measurents ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(521.76pt, 116.4pt, "3 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 143.04pt, "PSD performance. This invention facilitated, amongst others, new projects of dual-particle (neutron and ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 162pt, "gamma-ray) imagers in homeland security (see e.g. [15]) and medicine [16]-[17] using arrangements of ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 180.96pt, "multiple plastic scintillator bars. The overall performance and imaging quality in such projects depend, ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 199.92pt, "among other things, on the scintillators’ light yield (affecting energy, time, and depth-of-interaction ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 218.88pt, "resolution in the bars) and on the neutron-gamma separation (usually quantified in a Figure of Merit – ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 237.84pt, "FOM) in the energy range of interest. In practical applications outside of laboratories the ruggedness and ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 256.8pt, "stability of detectors against environmental factors as temperature variations or mechanical stress is also ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 275.76pt, "a major factor. Here, PU-based scintillators have a clear advantage over OGS [18]. This was our ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 294.72pt, "motivation to continue exploring PU-based scintillator recipes, to improve their performance, and to ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 313.68pt, "finally tap their full potential. ")
  #line-at(81.6pt, 338.64pt, "This paper demonstrates the progress made with PU-based scintillators. It compares the latest PU-")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 357.6pt, "based scintillator material named M700 with the older version M600, and with the common commercial ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 376.56pt, "materials EJ-200 (for general use) and EJ-276D (providing PSD and an improved stability). Comparative ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 395.52pt, "measurements of light yield and PSD performance have been made before and after the scintillator ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 414.48pt, "samples were arbitrarily aged by “steaming” in a hot and humid atmosphere, followed by freezing in a ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 433.44pt, "refrigerator. This procedure was chosen to include the aspect of ruggedness in the evaluation, and to ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 452.4pt, "evidence the robustness of PU-based materials. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 495.36pt, "2.")
  #line-at(80.906pt, 495.36pt, "Materials and methods ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 525.84pt, "2.1.")
  #line-at(87.378pt, 525.84pt, "Production of the PU-based scintillator samples ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(81.6pt, 550.56pt, "Scintillator samples of the PU-based materials M600 and M700 were produced inhouse at Rapiscan ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 569.52pt, "Systems’ (former Target Systemelektronik’s) production site in Wuppertal.  ")
  #line-at(81.6pt, 594.48pt, "For the preparation of M600, 30 wt% PPO (2,5-diphenyloxazole) and 0.2 wt% Bis-MSB (1,4-bis(2-")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 613.44pt, "methylstyryl)benzene) – each relative to the total mass – were completely dissolved in the resin ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 632.4pt, "component. The curing agent was then added, and the reaction mixture was homogenized under stirring. ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 651.36pt, "The resulting formulation was transferred into a silicone mold, degassed under vacuum, and ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 670.32pt, "subsequently cured at 100 °C for 72 h. ")
]

