#original-page(595.2pt, 841.92pt, (image("graphics/page-04.png", width: 51.5pt), 410.5pt, 266.5pt))[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(228.055pt, 116.4pt, "Paper submitted to ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(290.047pt, 116.4pt, "Radiation Measurement ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 116.4pt, "4 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(81.6pt, 143.04pt, "The preparation of M700 followed an analogous procedure. In this case, however, 30 wt% m-")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 162pt, "terphenyl and 0.2 wt% E404 [2,2′-bis(7-(2,2-dimethylpropyl)-9,9-dipropyl-9H-fluoren-2-yl)-1,4-")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 180.96pt, "benzene] were used instead of PPO and Bis-MSB. All subsequent steps – including dissolution in the ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 199.92pt, "resin component, addition of the curing agent, homogenization, casting into a silicone mold, vacuum ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 218.88pt, "degassing, and curing at 100 °C for 72 h – were identical to the procedure described above. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 249.12pt, "2.2.")
  #line-at(87.378pt, 249.12pt, "Scintillator materials investigated ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(81.6pt, 274.56pt, "In addition to the M600 and M700 scintillators prepared inhouse, two ")
  #line-at(419.148pt, 274.56pt, "26 mm ")
  #line-at(462.31pt, 274.56pt, " 26 mm-sized ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 294pt, "samples of common plastic scintillator materials – namely EJ-200 (general use, no PSD) and EJ-276D ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 312.96pt, "(providing PSD capabilities) – were purchased from Eljen Technology")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(387.6pt, 308.4pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(391.198pt, 312.96pt, ". The general properties of all ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 331.92pt, "materials involved in this investigation are compiled in ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(314.603pt, 331.92pt, "Table 1.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 362.16pt, "2.3.")
  #line-at(87.378pt, 362.16pt, "Preparation and ageing of scintillator samples for the comparative measurements ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(81.6pt, 386.88pt, "All scintillators, including the M600 and M700 samples prepared as described in 2.1, were cut to ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 405.84pt, "10 mm height. The scintillator faces were sanded in several stages to at least 1500 grit, and finally ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 424.8pt, "polished to high gloss surface using a soft cloth disc. This in-house preparation warranted the same size ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 443.76pt, "and surface quality of all samples (Fig. 1a). ")
  #line-at(81.6pt, 468.72pt, "After performing an initial set of characterization measurements with the fresh samples, the ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 487.68pt, "scintillators were arbitrarily aged. First, they were packed in a temperature-controlled electrical cooking ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 506.88pt, "pot that was partially filled with water. A glass stand prevented the samples from directly touching the ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 525.84pt, "water level. The samples were “steamed” for 48 hours at 60°C with the lid closed, which ensures a ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 544.8pt, "relative humidity around 100 %. The ageing was continued by exposing all samples for 48 hours to ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 563.76pt, "– 18°C in a refrigerator. Finally, photographs were taken (Figure 1b). The EJ-200 and EJ-276D samples ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 582.72pt, "appeared clouded and milky, while the M600 and M700 looked undisturbed and transparent as before. ")
  #line-at(81.6pt, 607.68pt, "This procedure is much shorter and less intense than the accelerated ageing process proposed and used ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 626.64pt, "in [20]. However, the visible differences in the scintillators’ appearance encouraged us to test their ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 645.6pt, "performance by another set of characterization measurements, with the intention to find differences in ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 664.56pt, "the scintillators’ response to environmental effects. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 695.28pt, "——— ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
