  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 142.32pt, "2.4.")
  #line-at(87.378pt, 142.32pt, "Characterization measurements ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(81.6pt, 167.04pt, "Relative light yield, energy resolution, and pulse-shape discrimination performance of the scintillator ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 186pt, "samples were determined at a test stand in Rapiscan Systems’ office in Wuppertal (Figure 2). The ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 204.96pt, "samples to be tested were not wrapped in any reflector but just fixed with optical grease (SilikonPaste ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 223.92pt, "1001 Professional by NASP Lubricants) in the center of the light-sensitive face of a photomultiplier tube ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 242.88pt, "(PMT). The tube, a Hamamatsu R10601-100 with a photocathode of 34 mm diameter, was standing in ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 261.84pt, "upright position. The PMT head with the sample attached (Figure 2a) was first covered with a solid ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 280.8pt, "Teflon-coated cup (serving as reflector for the light leaving the scintillator) and a lightproof outer skin, ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 299.76pt, "then fitted with a tailored mu-metal shield and mounted in a protecting aluminum tube (Figure 2b), and ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 318.72pt, "finally concealed with a flexible mesh reducing high-frequency electromagnetic interferences (visible in ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 337.68pt, "Figure 2b). The voltage divider board was designed to provide very stable dynode voltages even at high ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 356.64pt, "PMT gain and fast, large current pulses. PMT output signals were tapped at the anode and the last dynode ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 376.32pt, "and fed AC-coupled (CR filter with 3 ")
  #line-at(240.08pt, 376.32pt, "s decay time) into two separate oscilloscope inputs. This provided ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 395.76pt, "separate trigger- and energy-signal channels. The input filters were set at 300 Mhz. ")
  #line-at(81.6pt, 420.72pt, "The scintillator was then simultaneously exposed to neutrons from an unmoderated ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(470.873pt, 416.16pt, "252")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(481.373pt, 420.72pt, "Cf source ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 439.68pt, "emitting about 70,000 neutrons per second, and to gamma rays from a 20 kBq ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(411.294pt, 435.12pt, "137")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(421.794pt, 439.68pt, "Cs source providing the ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 458.88pt, "reference spectrum for energy calibration. Gamma rays from the ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(357.353pt, 454.32pt, "252")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(367.853pt, 458.88pt, "Cf source were shielded with a lead ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 477.84pt, "block of 20 mm thickness. The source-to-sample distances were adjusted to 10 cm. The dominating share ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 496.8pt, "of signals was due to ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(167.157pt, 492.24pt, "137")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(177.657pt, 496.8pt, "Cs gamma rays. During exposure, the PMT anode current signal was sampled ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 515.76pt, "with a Teledyne LeCroy HDO6054-MS digital oscilloscope, triggered by the last-dynode signal, and ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 534.72pt, "stored on disk. The sampling rate was set to 2.5 GS/s; one pulse record comprised 2,500 samples or ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 553.68pt, "1,000 ns at 12 bit resolution with a pre-trigger range of about 200 ns. Four hours of data collection, ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 572.88pt, "providing around 5")
  #set text(font: "Cambria Math", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(152.925pt, 572.88pt, "00,000")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(185.635pt, 572.88pt, " valid current pulses, were sufficient to characterize a single sample for energy ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 591.84pt, "depositions up to 1 MeVee (MeV electron equivalent). ")
  #line-at(81.6pt, 616.8pt, "For all measurements, the PMT position and orientation in the lab, the PMT voltage, and the ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 636pt, "oscilloscope settings were kept constant. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 666.24pt, "2.5.")
  #line-at(87.378pt, 666.24pt, "Data analysis ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(81.6pt, 690.96pt, "The data sets were analyzed offline with a dedicated Matlab script.  ")
]

