  #line-at(69.6pt, 143.04pt, "in identical geometries and under identical readout conditions. Light yields and energy resolutions of the ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 162pt, "materials investigated are quite similar. Moreover, the analysis focuses on relative light yields. Under ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 180.96pt, "these conditions, a low-order rational function provides a flexible yet well-constrained parametric ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 199.92pt, "representation of the Compton edge’s shape: It captures the necessary curvature and asymmetry without ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 218.88pt, "over-parameterization, while remaining numerically stable under noise and limited statistics. In ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 237.84pt, "extensive internal testing, we found that the three-zero/two-pole form represents the local edge region ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 256.8pt, "robustly across different scintillator materials, count rates, and acquisition conditions, while avoiding the ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 275.76pt, "strong parameter correlations commonly observed in higher-order polynomial or spline fits. The reversal ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 294.72pt, "point of this rational function is uniquely defined and reproducible, making it well suited as an ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 313.68pt, "operational definition of the Compton-edge reference point. ")
  #line-at(81.6pt, 338.64pt, "Therefore, the edge is fitted with a rational function comprising three zeros and two poles, and the ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 358.08pt, "reversal point of this function is taken as the reference point ")
