  #line-at(141.483pt, 406.32pt, " distributions in an energy window comprising the 477 keV reference Compton edge, ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 425.28pt, "and FOM dependencies on the energy deposition derived from slicing the PSD plot in the full energy ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 444.24pt, "range of interest and fitting the resulting FOMs with a rational function comprising three zeros and two ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 463.2pt, "poles, are shown in Figure 4. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 10.08pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 493.44pt, "2.6.")
  #line-at(87.378pt, 493.44pt, "Uncertainties ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(81.6pt, 518.16pt, "To estimate the uncertainty of relative light yields obtained with this procedure, a reproducibility test ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 537.12pt, "was performed after the initial characterization measurements. The EJ-200 sample was six times ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 556.32pt, "mounted on the PMT as described in section 2.4, measured with the respective procedure and the same ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 575.28pt, "statistics as in the characterization runs, and then removed from the PMT. The tests were performed on ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 594.24pt, "different days during a week. The Compton edge position was determined as described above. The ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 613.2pt, "statistical uncertainties of the Compton-edge positions, derived from uncertainties of the fit parameters ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 632.16pt, "provided by the fit procedure, was in the range of 1.7 to 2.2 % with an average of 1.97 %. The standard ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 651.12pt, "deviation of the Compton-edge positions obtained in the six runs was only 0.74 %, i.e., smaller than the ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 670.08pt, "statistical uncertainty estimate. Therefore, we assume an uncertainty of 2.0 % for the relative light yield ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 689.04pt, "determination. ")
]

