  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 143.04pt, "needed for mechanical processing. Further investigations should also include self-absorption effects ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 162pt, "which are important for applications in RPMs or large-area neutron imagers, as they degrade the ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 180.96pt, "performance of large-size scintillators. Altogether it would be very useful to include PU-based ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 199.92pt, "scintillators in future studies targeting the usability, ruggedness, and long-term stability of organic ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 218.88pt, "scintillators in various applications. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 261.84pt, "4.")
  #line-at(80.906pt, 261.84pt, "Applications of PU-based scintillators ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(81.6pt, 286.8pt, "PU-based scintillators, especially the latest version M700, are suitable materials for neutron or dual-")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 305.76pt, "particle (neutron and gamma-ray) imagers as they combine competitive PSD performance with ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 324.72pt, "mechanical robustness and ruggedness. Bar-shaped M600 and M700 scintillators fitting with the design ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 343.68pt, "of NOVO")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(115.68pt, 339.12pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(119.178pt, 343.68pt, ", a modular detector array for simultaneous neutron and gamma-ray imaging in cancer ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 362.64pt, "treatments with proton beams [16], have already been produced [18] and will be tested soon under ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 381.6pt, "realistic treatment conditions in a proton therapy center. A first imaging experiment was already ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 400.56pt, "performed at an accelerator-based  neutron source, using a provisional setup comprising OGS and M600 ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 420.24pt, "scintillator bars of the same size (12")
  #line-at(239.188pt, 420.24pt, "12")
  #line-at(256.225pt, 420.24pt, "140 mm")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(292.588pt, 415.68pt, "3")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(296.088pt, 420.24pt, "), read out on both sides with Hamamatsu S14161-")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 439.68pt, "3050HS-04 silicon photomultiplier (SiPM) arrays coupled to frontend electronics by Target ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 458.88pt, "Systemelektronik [21]. The results confirmed the detector concept as well as the usability of both ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 477.84pt, "scintillator materials, OGS and M600, for the NOVO project. ")
  #line-at(81.6pt, 502.8pt, "Another obvious application is radiation protection and dosimetry. The oxygen and nitrogen content ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 521.76pt, "of PU-based scintillators makes their response more body-equivalent than that of classic plastic ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 540.72pt, "scintillators, meaning their integrated signal (the total light produced in the scintillators) in reference ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 559.68pt, "gamma radiation fields better approaches the energy dependence of the dose absorbed by a human body. ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 578.64pt, "This suggests using this material for dose monitoring. Corresponding explorations are in progress. ")
  #line-at(81.6pt, 603.6pt, "Generally, PU-based scintillators could replace other plastics if the higher density and ruggedness are ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 622.56pt, "of importance. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 695.28pt, "——— ")
  #set text(font: "Arial", size: 6pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
