  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 7.92pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 116.4pt, "12 ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(69.6pt, 143.04pt, "5.")
  #line-at(80.906pt, 143.04pt, "Conclusions ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(81.6pt, 168pt, "This paper compares small samples of two polyurethane-based scintillator materials – the older M600 ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 186.96pt, "and the recent M700 by Rapiscan Systems – with Eljen EJ-276D, an up-to-date commercial plastic ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 205.92pt, "scintillator with neutron-gamma discrimination capabilities. M700 provides the best PSD performance ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 224.88pt, "and about the same light yield as EJ-276D, while its light pulses exhibit a shorter pulse decay. This ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 243.84pt, "qualifies the material for high-rate applications. The accelerated ageing process applied in this work was ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 262.8pt, "too short to trigger distinct performance degradation in any of the materials, though optical degradation ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 281.76pt, "was already visible. Nevertheless, the extremely robust polyurethane matrix promises advantages in ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 300.72pt, "resilience and long-term performance. PU-based scintillators should thus be included in future usability ")
  #line-at(69.6pt, 319.68pt, "studies of organic scintillators in various applications. ")
]

